    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` pipeline's audit step now emits an **immutable structured event** through the `AUDIT` logger, in addition to the existing human-readable audit line.\n\n**`AuditOwnerCreated`** (`rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`) \u2014 after logging the audit line, builds and logs an event:\n```\n{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n- `seq` comes from a process-wide `AtomicLong`, so it's **monotonically increasing across creates**.\n- The single-arg `AUDIT.info(String)` logs the JSON literally (no SLF4J `{}` substitution), and it stays inside the transaction-governed step so it fires only on a committed create.\n\n**`OwnerCreatedEvent`** (new record) \u2014 an immutable value object holding `seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel` plus the constant `event:'OWNER_CREATED'`, with self-contained JSON rendering (including proper string escaping). Immutability means the event can't be mutated after construction.\n\n**`Owner.getPrimaryIdentifier()`** (new accessor) \u2014 returns `customerCode` today. The event sources its carried identifier from this one method rather than from `getCustomerCode()` directly. That satisfies the forward-looking requirement: **when the customerCode is later unified into a memberId, repointing this single accessor moves every emitted event onto the memberId** without touching the event or audit code.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier` (asserting one `AUDIT` line contains `OWNER_CREATED`, the owner id, and the customerCode) passes, and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
